# Local REST-client examples. Fill variables with your own local credentials.
# Keep actual passwords, access tokens and invite codes out of version control.
@base = http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/v1
@email = replace@example.test
@password = REPLACE_WITH_A_LOCAL_PASSWORD
@accessToken = REPLACE_FROM_LOGIN_RESPONSE
@inviteCode = REPLACE_FROM_CREATE_RESPONSE
@loungeId = REPLACE_FROM_CREATE_RESPONSE

### Register
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"{{email}}","password":"{{password}}","displayName":"Local listener"}

### Login (client must retain refresh cookie)
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email":"{{email}}","password":"{{password}}"}

### Catalog
GET {{base}}/tracks?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Create (use a new UUID for a different request)
POST {{base}}/lounges
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Command-Id: 9e628b81-2c19-4f15-801a-5bb4e760e259
Content-Type: application/json

{"seedTrackId":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001","vibeProfile":"After Hours","maxParticipants":10,"bpmTolerancePct":8,"soundclashEnabled":true,"aiVerbosity":"normal"}

### Join using the second user's access token
POST {{base}}/lounges/join
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"inviteCode":"{{inviteCode}}"}

### Snapshot (membership required)
GET {{base}}/lounges/{{loungeId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Refresh with retained cookie
POST {{base}}/auth/refresh
Origin: http://127.0.0.1:5173
X-CSRF-Protection: 1

### Logout with retained cookie
POST {{base}}/auth/logout
Origin: http://127.0.0.1:5173
X-CSRF-Protection: 1
